cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DesiredGainR, cite the software and the method implemented in your analysis."
title: "DesiredGainR: Desired-Gain Selection Index and Quadratic Genomic Selection Index Tools for Plant Breeding"
type: software
version: 0.5.0
authors:
  - family-names: Akohoue
    given-names: Félicien
    email: akohoue.f@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2160-0182"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/FAkohoue/DesiredGainR"
url: "https://FAkohoue.github.io/DesiredGainR/"
abstract: >
  Multi-trait selection index tools organised around the breeding objective
  rather than around the index. DesiredGainR translates exactly between
  economic weights and desired gains, tests whether a stated objective is
  attainable at the planned selection intensity, recovers the objective a
  programme has been applying implicitly from its historical selection
  differentials, and reports how far a decision depends on weights that are
  themselves uncertain. It provides the classical index families, the
  iterative desired-gain index, and the quadratic genomic selection index,
  together with a multi-cycle simulation layer whose founders are built from
  the breeder's own phased marker data rather than from a simulated genome.
keywords:
  - plant breeding
  - selection index
  - desired gain
  - economic weights
  - multi-trait selection
  - genomic selection
